{
  "_about": [
    "PCFD CAD vocabulary: everything the console offers as a list, in one file, read at startup.",
    "From the department's sheet \"[TEMPLATE] PCFD ECC OPS\" (export of 2026-10-07): codes, order, statuses and",
    "colors. Each item is {code, name}: the code is the sheet's (stored, matched, exported to CSV), the name is",
    "what the console shows. A plain string is also accepted (code = name). Keys starting with _ are notes.",
    "The department's own code sheet (2026-10-07, dept_codes) adds the unit status codes (AQ, AV, DP ... OS),",
    "every unit by department, the MA codes, the misc codes and a type -> subtype map to MVA (the rest to confirm). Codes",
    "are the identity: a code shows as itself until it is named (Settings). Names are filled only where the",
    "meaning is clear (E60 Engine 60, 2398 23 98); everything else stays a bare code, marked \"meaning to",
    "confirm\" in Settings, like an item with a confirm note here (\"confirm\": why).",
    "Still guesses: names whose meaning is unclear are left as the code (ECHO, AIR, MULTI, NEXT, CAD, RMA;",
    "TRANS, CO-NO and CO-YES were confirmed by PCFD); the unit status roles (see _unit_statuses); event_class,",
    "unit kinds/spares, received_via, run cards, spoken phrases and geo_town_order.",
    "These are the defaults: edits made in the console's Settings are kept in the CAD database, laid over",
    "this file (sizeup/cad/settings.py). version: shown in Settings > System; bump it when the file changes."
  ],
  "version": "2026-10-07.4",
